{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>For their rock is not like our Rock.</b> And this happened without doubt because their rock is not like our Rock. For indeed every nation prospers all the days of the rule of its prince or its constellation, and that prince will never be turned into an enemy of his people. But they fall when the rule of the prince ceases, and when the prince of another nation rules, according to the order that the blessed El established among them. And therefore they are not destroyed in a manner contrary to nature until one pursues a thousand." "<b>And our enemies.</b> Even though the Chaldeans were enemies of HaShem and enemies of His people, as He testified in saying לוּלֵי כַּעַס אוֹיֵב אָגוּר (Deuteronomy 32:27), and in saying מֵרֹאשׁ פַּרְעוֹת אוֹיֵב (Deuteronomy 32:42)." "<b>פְּלִילִים.</b> These are the masters of intellectual deliberations in statecraft, as it says וְהַאֲבַדְתִּי חֲכָמִים מֵאֱדוֹם (Obadiah 1:8) — by implication, they exist."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:16.024409055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}